-- title:
--   Labelled presentation on a connected basic open at each prime
-- statement:
--   The data of the statement fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Numerical and arithmetic base data.** Two primes $r$, $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, the hypothesis that $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete, that $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and that $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$; a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, subject to: $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$. A monoid homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$, i.e. $vdet$ is the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternionic moduli frame.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ divides $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point map $pt$ assigning to each ring $S$, each $\mathcal O$-point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ and each fake elliptic curve over $S$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure a section over $s$, and `h𝒳` asserting that this makes $\mathcal X$ a coarse moduli space (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map $ptF$ and `hM` asserting that $M$ is a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure; a group $G$, a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and a labelling $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ with `hρ` asserting that $\rho$ realises the twisting action of level labels on $M$ (compatibility over the base, the twist equation, multiplicativity of $\chi$ modulo $n$, and bijectivity of $\chi$ modulo $n$ onto the invertible residues). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`), compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$: a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map $ptT$ and `h𝒴` asserting it is a coarse moduli space for curves carrying an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup; two degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), with $d_0$ forgetting the extra structure (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ computing the $\ell$-isogenous curve (`hd₁`). Two endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \otimes \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v \mid \bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; the height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma^{t}$ of units characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all primes other than $v$. Families $s_\ell$ (global units) and $sf_\ell$ (adelic units) indexed by the primes $\ell \neq r, \bar r$, with `hs` (four clauses): away from $r$ the $\ell$-datum $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell \otimes 1$, at $r$ it has component $1$, the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; the groups $\Gamma^{t}_\ell = \Gamma^{t} \cap s_\ell \Gamma^{t} s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Special-fibre data.** The hypothesis $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`) and a coordinate map $coord : \Lambda \to \mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace condition). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over that residue ring (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ in two variables with `hA₀` identifying the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $coord$; maps $e, e' : \Gamma^{t} \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $deg$. The clauses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'` state that each $e(\gamma)$, $e'(\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{deg \gamma}$ preserving the level structure, that $e$ is multiplicative up to powers of $r$, that scalar $\gamma$ give scalar isogenies up to powers of $r$, and conversely that $\gamma$ is scalar whenever $e(\gamma)$ is. The clause `hE2` states that for every injective ring embedding of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and of $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e(\gamma)$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$. The clause `hE3` provides, for each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$, labels $lab : \Gamma^{t} \to \Lambda$ computing the action of $e(\gamma)$ on that structure, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$. The clause `hE4` states that over algebraically closed fields every degree-$r^d$ level-preserving isogeny pair of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e(\gamma)$ up to powers of $r$. A suborder $R_2 \leq R_1$ (`hR₂o`) with $r$-power saturation in $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) together with $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base, and the clauses `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e`: $\hat e$ is additive on points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level structure; it is unital, multiplicative, and agrees with the $\Lambda$-action on integers; $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by the reduced norm; $\hat e$ agrees with $e$ up to powers of $r$; and the matrix normalisation of `hE2` can be chosen simultaneously for $\Gamma^{t}$ and for $R_2$.
--
--   **Drinfeld-side data.** A ring map $\iota : \mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2}) \to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses): on admissible rigidified objects $\eta$ identifies points exactly with isomorphism classes, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every point of $MD$ is, locally on a finite cover of the base by basic opens, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$. An injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and of $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is, up to a fixed power $r^{m}$, exactly the integral matrices (`hE₀`). A family of maps $eD$ together with `hnatD` (naturality in the base), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (compatibility with the dictionary leg), `hGLD` ($\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-equivariance: the action on $MD$-points corresponds to the twisted action on pairs consisting of a leg and a Deligne datum), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to twisting the leg by $Fr$, and $\pi$-translates exist); these identify the functor of $MD$-points over $\mathcal O$ with the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ and the formal upper half-plane functor $\Omega$ attached to $(K_0,\pi)$. A ring map $\kappa : Onr/(\pi) \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **Base point, Atkin–Lehner datum and the map $\Xi$.** A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/(\pi)$ together with $aw$, $aw'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), and $bw$, $bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level structure (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), with the normalisation `hJOINTw` extending `hE2` to the composite $aw \circ bw$ with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ in place of $\iota_0(\gamma)$. A map $\Xi$ assigning to each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over a connected base the dictionary leg of $\Xi$ is an integral $Fr$-twist of the given leg), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under comparison isomorphisms of rigidified curves) and `hΞdef` (over a connected base with $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed by the admissible rigidified object transported along $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with an exponent $j \leq 1$, and its leg is the $(-j)$-fold $Fr$-twist). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` and `heqW`: translating a rigidification by $e(\gamma)$, respectively passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (when $\bar r$ is invertible in the base), corresponds under $\Xi$ to the action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$, respectively of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$, for some integer $c$.
--
--   **The relative point functor of rigidified curves.** A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`) together with $\chi_C : Onr \to C$; a functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras; a point map $ptR$ sending a $C$-algebra $S$ with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure, a leg $\psi_S$ equal to the base change of $\chi_C$, a fake elliptic curve with full level-$n$ structure over $S$ and a rigidification of it to an element of $PR(S)$; and the laws `hR2` (compatibility of $ptR$ with pullback along $C$-algebra maps), `hR3s` (every element of $PR(S)$ is $ptR$ of some pair), `hR3i` (over a connected base, equality of two values of $ptR$ forces an isomorphism of the level structures together with a comparison of the rigidifications up to powers of $r$) and `hR1` (the converse: such an isomorphism and comparison force equality of the two values of $ptR$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every Noetherian $C$-algebra $S$ with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure, every $x \in PR(S)$ and every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $S$, there exists $c \in S$ with $c \notin \mathfrak p$ such that
--
--   1. every idempotent of the localisation $S[1/c]$ is $0$ or $1$ (that is, $\operatorname{Spec} S[1/c]$ is connected), and
--
--   2. there exist $g \in G$ and $j \in \{0,1\}$ for which the following hold: $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S[1/c]$, and there are a leg $\psi_S : Onr \to S[1/c]$ equal to the composite of $\chi_C$ with the structure map $C \to S[1/c]$, a fake elliptic curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S[1/c]$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of its underlying curve relative to $A_0$ and $\psi_S$, such that
--    * $ptR(u,\rho)$ equals the image of $x$ under $PR$ applied to the localisation map $S \to S[1/c]$;
--    * there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on the underlying curve of $u$ which is a normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ (the predicate `IsNormLevelTransport` for $Fr$, $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$, $\Phi$, $\iota$, $coord$), and the given level structure of $u$ is the translate of $P_n$ by the action of $\chi(g)$;
--    * the dictionary leg of $\Xi$ applied to the rigidified curve $(u_1,\rho)$ over $S[1/c]$ equals the $(-j)$-fold $Fr$-twist of $\psi_S$.
--
--   This is the local step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison at which a point of the functor of rigidified fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure is presented, after passing to a connected basic open neighbourhood of a given prime, by an explicit curve together with a rigidification, a level structure transported from the base point $P_0$ and twisted by a group label $g$, and a Frobenius exponent $j \in \{0,1\}$ recording the dictionary leg. It feeds the statement that such labels are natural, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr).
